title: $:/themes/nikorion/pkm/language/en-GB/readme
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

A Vanilla-based TiddlyWiki theme with a personal look: the author's stylesheets and the overrides of third-party shadow tiddlers (Vanilla theme settings, Kookma plugins), gathered in one plugin instead of being scattered as loose tiddlers of the wiki.

! What it is

A complete theme (plugin type //theme//). The PKM Palette plugin selects it (`$:/theme`); otherwise select it in //Control Panel → Appearance → Theme//. It builds on Vanilla, which stays loaded as a dependency (nothing is copied), and adds the author's setting values, stylesheets and overrides on top. Colours come from the palette (see the PKM Palette plugin). The layout is not provided: use any layout (Layout for instance).

! What it changes

|!Part |!Tiddlers |
|Body text |`$:/themes/nikorion/pkm/styles/body-text`: foreground and background colours, Inter font, no ligatures in code |
|Headings |`$:/themes/nikorion/pkm/styles/headings`: Palatino headings with rules, site title |
|Rules |`$:/themes/nikorion/pkm/styles/hr`: `<hr>` with a central logo (logo shipped with the plugin) |
|Code highlighting |`$:/themes/nikorion/pkm/styles/highlight`: Obsidian colours for highlight.js |
|Frames |`$:/themes/nikorion/pkm/styles/layout-vanilla`: tiddler frame and sidebar borders |
|Coloured blocks |`$:/themes/nikorion/pkm/styles/infobox`: `info0`, `interro0`, `alert0` classes |
|Vanilla settings |font families, sizes, sidebar width, background image (shipped with the plugin), sticky titles |
|Third-party overrides |Kookma Refnotes footnote counter, Kookma Tweaks headings (emptied), Shiraz Formatter highlight colours |

! Loading order

The plugin declares `plugin-priority` 100. TiddlyWiki registers the shadow tiddlers of plugins in ascending priority, the last one winning: the core has 0, ordinary plugins and themes 1, so this plugin always overrides them, whatever their alphabetical order.

! Requirements

* The Vanilla theme must be listed in the wiki's themes (it is, by default).
* The [[PKM Palette|https://github.com/nikorion/TW-PKM-Palette]] plugin: the theme holds no colour, it reads the palette keys as CSS variables.

* TiddlyWiki >= 5.3.5.
* The fonts //Inter//, //Palatino Linotype// and //JetBrains Mono// are not shipped: install them on the machine or with the Font Manager plugin.
